[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100888,
      "id": "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a",
      "title": "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ad45a7ac-27a0-59f4-8130-e8b4e6e753ed",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=- 6 e^{\\frac{y}{3}},\\qquad 3 x - 4>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 4 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- \\frac{12}{3 x - 4}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 4 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 4 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-3\\cdot\\frac{3}{3 x - 4} \\\\ &=- \\frac{9}{3 x - 4} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{12}{3 x - 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 4 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- \\frac{9}{3 x - 4}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 6 e^{\\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ - \\frac{9}{3 x - 4} &\\overset{?}{=}-6e^{-(- 3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 4 \\right)})/(-3)} \\\\ - \\frac{9}{3 x - 4} &\\overset{?}{=}-6e^{-\\ln(3 x - 4)} \\\\ - \\frac{9}{3 x - 4} &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{6}{3 x - 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 4 \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ea6922d6-ff6b-5c97-8cbc-6fdde5c4435a",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
